     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Oli,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for your contribution to hBayesDM!</div><div><br></div><div>Those Python codes (convert-to-r.py and convert-to-py.py) use `pathlib.Path` to handle file paths. However, it seems that Python 3.5 has an unexpected incompatibility with it.</div><div><br></div><div>Instead, I just checked that it perfectly works with Python 3.6 and above. Could you set up your Python environment with a higher version and try it out?</div><div><br></div><div>I will edit the contribution wiki page as it requires Python 3.6 or above, too. Sorry for your inconvenience.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Jaeyeong</div></div>"
